The '''2025–26 Ligue 2''', commonly known as '''Ligue 2 [[Balkrishna Industries|BKT]]''' for sponsorship reasons, is the 87th season of [[Ligue 2]]. The season began on 9 August 2025 and concluded on 8 May 2026.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.lfp.fr/article/publication-du-calendrier-general-de-la-ligue-2-bkt-pour-la-saison-2025-2026|title=PUBLICATION DU CALENDRIER GÉNÉRAL DE LA LIGUE 2 BKT POUR LA SAISON 2025/2026|date=4 March 2025 |publisher=lfp.fr|access-date=2 May 2025|language=fr}}</ref>

== Overview ==
=== Promoted and relegation teams (pre-season) ===
[[FC Lorient]] and [[Paris FC]] were promoted to [[Ligue 1]] after one and seven years in Ligue 2, respectively.<ref>{{cite web |title=Lorient return to Ligue 1 after one season |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/lorient-return-ligue-1-after-one-season-2025-04-26/#:~:text=April%2026%20(Reuters)%20%2D%20Ligue,campaign%20when%20they%20finished%2017th. |publisher=Reuters |access-date=6 July 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=A second Paris football club has reached France's first division |url=https://www.lemonde.fr/en/sports/article/2025/05/03/a-second-paris-football-club-has-reached-france-s-first-division_6740867_9.html#:~:text=Six%20months%20after%20being%20bought,establish%20a%20lasting%20presence%20there.&text=Pierre%20Ferracci%20had%20been%20waiting%20for%20this%20moment%20for%2013%20years. |publisher=Le Monde |access-date=6 July 2025}}</ref>

[[FC Metz|Metz]] was promoted to Ligue 1 after defeating [[Stade de Reims|Reims]] in the Ligue 1 promotion/relegation play-offs after one year in the second tier. Reims will be relegated to a lower division after a 7-year tenure in the top flight.<ref>{{cite web |title=FC Metz Earns Promotion to Ligue 1 After Impressive Extra Time Win |url=https://ligue1.com/articles/l1_article_2643-fc-metz-earns-promotion-to-ligue-1-after-impressive-extra-time-win |publisher=Ligue 1 |access-date=6 July 2025}}</ref>

[[Montpellier HSC|Montpellier]] and [[AS Saint-Étienne|Saint-Étienne]] will return to Ligue 2 after sixteen years and one year being in Ligue 1, respectively.<ref>{{cite web |title=The Leicester of Ligue 1: Remembering Montpellier's famous title triumph on the day of their relegation |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/montpellier-ligue-1-relegation-leicester-city-b2748143.html |publisher=The Independent |access-date=6 July 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Saint-Étienne relegated to Ligue 2, Reims to face Metz in the playoffs either side of the Coupe de France final |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/article/saint-etienne-relegated-ligue-2-212700308.html |publisher=Yahoo Sports |access-date=6 July 2025}}</ref>

[[AS Nancy Lorraine|Nancy]], [[Le Mans FC|Le Mans]] and [[US Boulogne|Boulogne]] will return to Ligue 2 from the [[Championnat National]] after three and five and thirteen years absence, respectively, with Boulogne's promotion being back-to-back from the [[Championnat National 2 (1993–2026)|Championnat National 2]] two seasons ago.

[[Stade Malherbe Caen|Caen]] were relegated to Championnat National after 6 years in the second tier and will play in the 3rd tier for the first time since 1984 and after a 41 year absence.<ref>{{cite web |title=Caen, owned by Kylian Mbappé, officially relegated to National 1 |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/article/caen-owned-kylian-mbapp-officially-201100615.html#:~:text=Owned%20by%20Kylian%20Mbappé%20since,the%20first%20time%20since%201984. |publisher=Yahoo Sports |access-date=6 July 2025}}</ref>

=== Administratively relegated team ===

[[FC Martigues|Martigues]] were excluded to [[French football league system|Régional 1]], the 6th tier of French football, and will play in regional football for the first time in 55 years.<ref>{{cite web |title=FC Martigues excluded from national competitions by the DNCG |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/article/official-fc-martigues-excluded-national-135500270.html |publisher=Yahoo Sports |access-date=6 July 2025}}</ref>

[[AC Ajaccio]] were relegated due to financial problems. They will return to the [[Championnat National]] after 27 years.<ref>{{cite web |title=Ajaccio provisionally demoted to National as City Group given potential lifeline |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/ajaccio-provisionally-demoted-national-city-082400641.html |publisher=Yahoo Sports |access-date=6 July 2025}}</ref> On 16 July 2025, the club relegation administratively is confirmed.

[[Olympique Lyonnais|Lyon]] had been administratively relegated to the league from highest tier on 23 June 2025, meaning Reims were due to be kept in the Ligue 1. The decision was later overturned on appeal from Lyon on 9 July, meaning both clubs competitively incurred places remain unchanged.<ref>{{cite web |title=Lyon win Ligue 1 relegation appeal: What this means for Crystal Palace and Nottingham Forest |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6449082/2025/07/09/lyon-relegation-decision-ligue-1/ |publisher=The Athletic |access-date=9 July 2025}}</ref>

